      "message": "Somehow this is defined as `uint16_t` in GCC:\nhttps://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc/blob/releases/gcc-14.2.0/gcc/config/arm/arm_neon.h#L10902\n\nI get the following compile error:\n``` \nIn file included from /deps/aom/aom_dsp/flow_estimation/arm/disflow_neon.c:17:\n/deps/aom/aom_dsp/arm/mem_neon.h:63:27: error: conflicting types for \u0027vld1q_s16_x4\u0027; have \u0027int16x8x4_t(const int16_t *)\u0027 {aka \u0027int16x8x4_t(const short int *)\u0027}\n   63 | static inline int16x8x4_t vld1q_s16_x4(const int16_t *ptr) {\n      |                           ^~~~~~~~~~~~\nIn file included from /deps/aom/aom_dsp/flow_estimation/arm/disflow_neon.c:14:\n/x-tools/armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf/lib/gcc/armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf/14.2.0/include/arm_neon.h:10902:1: note: previous definition of \u0027vld1q_s16_x4\u0027 with type \u0027int16x8x4_t(const uint16_t *)\u0027 {aka \u0027int16x8x4_t(const short unsigned int *)\u0027}\n10902 | vld1q_s16_x4 (const uint16_t * __a)\n      | ^~~~~~~~~~~~\n```\n\nWhich I could workaround with:\n```\nsed -i \"/vld1q_s16_x4/s/int16_t/u\u0026/g\" aom_dsp/arm/mem_neon.h\n```\n\ni.e. doing this:\n```suggestion\nstatic inline int16x8x4_t vld1q_s16_x4(const uint16_t *ptr) {\n```\n\nfor all `vld1q_s16_x4()` inline decls in this file.",
